	[Documentation]  1135614 - Verify the version changes when create and republishing the workflow multiple times
	...      Verify the information is saved correctly when create a new workflow
	...      Verify the error message when user try to publish the workflow in INIT status
	...      Verify the error message when user try to publish the workflow in published status
	...      Verify the error message when user try to save the workflow in Published status
	...      Verify the error message when create workflow with no access token
	...      Verify the error message when create workflow with expired token
	...      Verify the version is updated correctly when user republish the workflow for multiple times
	[Tags]  WorkFlowVersionControl  FlowZero  DesignWorkflow  Regression
	GROUP  Create a new workflow and check the information
	    comment  ======Step1: Create a draft workflow and check the information is saved correctly
	    # Create draft
	    ${req_host}  Set Variable  ${URL}
	    ${req_header_admin}  Create Dictionary  Single-Ui-Authorization=${token_admin}
	    ${CountryCodes}     Get Random Countries Or BusinessArea     Countries
	    ${BusinessArea}      Get Random Countries Or BusinessArea     BusinessArea
        ${WFName}  randomString  20  lm
        ${WFName_Original}    Set Variable      AutoTest ${WFName}
        ${Description}  randomString  500  lm
	    ${req_body}   Create Dictionary   name=${WFName_Original}  countryCodes=${CountryCodes}  businessArea=${BusinessArea}  createdBy=${USERNAME_WF_ADMIN}  icon=${HeadIcon1}  description=${Description}
	    FOR  ${i}  IN RANGE  1
		    RequestsLibrary.Create Session  website  url=${req_host}
		    ${response}  RequestsLibrary.Post On Session    website    url=api/ratan/api/v1/workflow/create    json=${req_body}	 headers=${req_header_admin} 	allow_redirects=${False}
	        ${create_utc_min}   Get Current Date   result_format=%Y-%m-%d %H:%M    time_zone=UTC
	    END
	    ${req_header_expired}     Create Dictionary  Single-Ui-Authorization=${token_expired}
	    ${req_header_noaccess}     Create Dictionary  Single-Ui-Authorization=${token_noaccess}
	    # Check the error message when create workflow with with expired token
	    FOR  ${i}  IN RANGE  1
		    RequestsLibrary.Create Session  website  url=${req_host}
		    ${response_error}  RequestsLibrary.Post On Session    website    url=api/ratan/api/v1/workflow/create    json=${req_body}	 headers=${req_header_expired}  	allow_redirects=${False}   expected_status=503
	    END
	    RequestsLibrary.Delete All Sessions
	    # Check the error message when create workflow with no access user
	    FOR  ${i}  IN RANGE  1
		    RequestsLibrary.Create Session  website  url=${req_host}
		    ${response_error}  RequestsLibrary.Post On Session    website    url=api/ratan/api/v1/workflow/create    json=${req_body}	 headers=${req_header_noaccess}  	allow_redirects=${False}   expected_status=403
	    END
        RequestsLibrary.Delete All Sessions
        Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  Should Contain  ${response_error.text}   ACTION_DENIED
